  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_10264",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of X-linked Adrenal Hypoplasia Congenita (X-AXH) through a chain of indications that link the drug to chronic adrenal insufficiency and, subsequently, to the condition. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone may be used in the management of conditions such as Inherited Isolated Adrenal Insufficiency Due To Partial Cyp11a1 Deficiency and Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, both of which are associated with X-AXH. This implies that Prednisolone may exert a role in modulating adrenal function, potentially through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood. The presence of a direct indication from Methylprednisolone to X-AXH further supports the hypothesis that Prednisolone could be a candidate for repurposing in this context. The mechanism of action remains unclear, but the observed indications suggest a possible involvement of adrenal function regulation. The evidence is consistent with a potential role of Prednisolone in the pathophysiology of X-AXH, though further mechanistic studies are needed to confirm this relationship.",
